{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>וְעָשִׂיתָ כַפֹּרֶת.</b> A covering from above — an allusion that one must cover the secrets of the Torah and not reveal them to the multitudes, for things that the Ancient of Days has covered — do not reveal them. And as it is written (Proverbs 11:13), ״וְנֶאֱמַן רוּחַ מְכַסֶּה דָבָר״, and it is written (ibid. 25:2), ״כְּבוֹד אֱלֹהִים הַסְתֵּר דָבָר״. And the two cherubim were in the likeness of angels, which are called cherubim, and in the likeness of small children, to teach that if the sage is like an angel of YHWH of Hosts and he is clean from sin like a child of one year, then they will seek Torah from his mouth. And he must be clean before both Elohim and man — for to satisfy Heaven, the cherubim spread their wings upward, and to satisfy creatures, their faces were turned one toward the other, which also points to the peace granted to the lovers of Torah, and they were together, matched in peace and fellowship. ״אֶל הַכַּפֹּרֶת יִהְיוּ פְּנֵי הַכְּרוּבִים״ — that the entire aim of their faces should be toward the Torah that is in the Ark, not like those who are wise in their own eyes and seek honor for themselves and not for the honor of the Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:03.590988221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}